6.3 SINGLE-TENANT ECS/EC2 (Non-Multitenant)
Each tenant receives a dedicated EC2 instance (m5.large or equivalent),
provisioned on-demand or reserved.

  Tenants    EC2 Instances    Monthly Cost (est.)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  6          6 dedicated      ~$150–$220
  10         10 dedicated     ~$250–$370
  15         15 dedicated     ~$370–$550

- No shared-host risk — strongest hardware isolation.
- On-demand scheduling reduces idle cost vs always-on clusters.
- Cost scales linearly with tenants — no economy of scale.
- Reserved instance pricing can reduce costs by 30–40%.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
6.4 COSMOS DBT + ASTRONOMER
Fully managed SaaS: Astronomer hosts orchestration; Cosmos dbt manages
the dbt runtime. Pricing is usage-billed per DAG run / compute hour.

  Tenants    Astronomer Plan           Est. Monthly Cost
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  1–6        Starter / Standard        ~$200–$400
  7–12       Standard                  ~$350–$700
  13–18      Standard / Enterprise     ~$600–$1,200+

- Highest per-run cost at low volume — offset by near-zero infra ops.
- Astronomer plan tier jumps introduce step-wise cost increases.
- Vendor lock-in risk: migration requires re-platforming orchestration.
- Best suited for teams prioritising speed-to-market over cost optimisation.

