10. KEY ASSUMPTIONS & SENSITIVITY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Costs and performance are sensitive to:
- Actual average runtime (30 vs 90 minutes changes totals materially)
- Task size (vCPU/memory) and concurrency peaks
- EC2 instance family/size, autoscaling, and utilisation %
- Astronomer plan tier and included compute hours
- Retries/reruns frequency
- Non-compute costs: logging, storage, NAT/egress, ECR pulls
- Reserved vs on-demand EC2 pricing (30–40% savings with reservations)

